<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Debug builds only. This file replaces the release policy in src/main because
  the debug source set of a library variant wins over main, and the app's debug
  variant consumes the library's debug variant.

  Why it has to exist at all: the licence server runs on Laragon over plain
  HTTP during development, and from Android 9 the platform refuses cleartext by
  default. The refusal surfaces as a thrown fetch, which `syncLicence` in
  `src/core/license.ts` deliberately treats as "no news" and logs at debug level
  — so without this the failure is indistinguishable from being offline, which
  is the single most expensive way for a network problem to present itself.
  A whole afternoon goes into "why does my server never get a request" when the
  request was never allowed to leave the phone.

  It permits cleartext to everything rather than to a named host on purpose. The
  phone cannot resolve `spool.pardeep.app` — that is a hosts-file entry on the
  developer's PC — so testing happens against whatever the LAN address of the
  moment is, or 10.0.2.2 from the emulator, and a domain allowlist would have to
  be edited every time the router hands out a new lease.

  It is not a hole in the shipped app: release builds get src/main's policy,
  which denies cleartext outright. Verify that after any change to the manifest
  merger by checking the merged manifest of a release build, not this file.
-->
<network-security-config>
  <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
    <trust-anchors>
      <certificates src="system" />
      <!--
        Lets a locally-generated CA (Laragon's SSL, mitmproxy, Charles) be
        trusted while debugging HTTPS. Debug only, and the release policy above
        has no such entry.
      -->
      <certificates src="user" />
    </trust-anchors>
  </base-config>
</network-security-config>
